WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.830
Add GPROXY as a provider in the Codex configuration file.

2
00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:10.692
Use the local base URL ending in slash v1, and set the wire API to
responses.

3
00:00:10.712 --> 00:00:14.612
Select a model route that already exists in the gateway.

4
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:21.692
Export the gateway key as the GPROXY_API_KEY environment variable named
in the configuration.

5
00:00:21.712 --> 00:00:24.988
The key is entered without displaying its value.

6
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.092
Run codex exec with a simple prompt.

7
00:00:29.112 --> 00:00:36.350
The terminal identifies GPROXY as the provider and receives a real
reply, confirming that the client is connected.
